  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nRadar indicating showers with some embedded downpours \ncontinuing to move SE across the area ahead of a cold front \napproaching from the west. Moist air mass in place with PWAT \naround 2.0\", will lower behind the front this morning. Drying \nconditions will occur today, with showers ending prior to \ndaybreak. Winds will shift to the W-NW, with gusts of 25-35 mph\ndeveloping, as forecast soundings indicating a good mixing \nenvironment. High temperatures will be warm ranging from around\n70F in the W. Adirondacks to mid 80s in the mid Hudson Valley. \nIt will still be humid this morning with dewpoints mainly in the\n60s, then gradually lowering this afternoon as drier air filters\nin.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHigh pressure building east across the region will bring cool, \ndry conditions Friday through early Saturday. As the high shifts\neast off the coast, a warmer southerly flow will start to \ndevelop Sat afternoon. Moisture will increase Sat night (PWAT \nanomalies rise to +1 to +2 STDEV), with a short wave approaching\nfrom the south/west bringing some showers, and perhaps an \nisolated thunderstorm, Sat night into Sunday morning. It will \nbecome more humid again, with dewpoints expected to rise into \nthe 60s on Sun. Additional scattered showers/T-storms may occur \non Sun ahead of a cold front that is expected to move through \nSun night. Drier and seasonably cooler temperatures then build \nin for early next week.",
